# MedicHub - GraphQL Request Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as Browser/Mobile
    participant Apollo as Apollo Client
    participant HTTP as HTTP/WebSocket
    participant Server as Apollo Server
    participant Middleware as Middleware Chain
    participant RateLimit as RateLimitGuard
    participant Auth as GqlAuthGuard
    participant Resolver as GraphQL Resolver
    participant Service as Business Service
    participant Prisma as Prisma ORM
    participant Redis as Redis Cache
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    %% Query Flow
    rect rgb(59, 130, 246, 0.1)
        Note over Client,DB: GraphQL Query Flow
        Client->>Apollo: Execute query/mutation
        Apollo->>Apollo: Add auth headers (cookie)
        Apollo->>Apollo: Serialize variables
        Apollo->>HTTP: POST /graphql

        HTTP->>Server: GraphQL request
        Server->>Middleware: Helmet (security headers)
        Middleware->>Middleware: i18next (language detection)
        Middleware->>Middleware: Body parser (JSON)
        Middleware->>Middleware: Cookie parser
        Middleware->>Middleware: Session middleware

        Server->>Server: Parse GraphQL query
        Server->>Server: Validate query syntax

        alt Rate Limited Endpoint
            Server->>RateLimit: Check rate limit
            RateLimit->>Redis: ZADD, ZCOUNT (sliding window)
            Redis-->>RateLimit: Attempt count

            alt Limit Exceeded
                RateLimit-->>Server: RateLimitException (429)
                Server-->>HTTP: Error response
                HTTP-->>Apollo: Rate limit error
                Apollo-->>Client: Show error (retry after X seconds)
            else Within Limit
                RateLimit-->>Server: Proceed
            end
        end

        alt Protected Endpoint
            Server->>Auth: @Authorization() decorator
            Auth->>Auth: Extract session from cookie
            Auth->>Redis: Get session data
            Redis-->>Auth: Session object

            alt Session Valid
                Auth->>Prisma: Find user by userId
                Prisma->>DB: SELECT FROM users WHERE id = ?
                DB-->>Prisma: User data
                Prisma-->>Auth: User object
                Auth->>Auth: Attach user to context
                Auth-->>Server: Authorized
            else Session Invalid
                Auth-->>Server: UnauthorizedException (401)
                Server-->>HTTP: Unauthorized response
                HTTP-->>Apollo: Auth error
                Apollo->>Apollo: Clear cache
                Apollo-->>Client: Redirect to login
            end
        end

        Server->>Resolver: Execute resolver
        Resolver->>Resolver: Extract decorators (@Lang, @Authorized, @UserAgent)
        Resolver->>Resolver: Validate DTOs (class-validator)

        alt Validation Failed
            Resolver-->>Server: BadRequestException (400)
            Server-->>HTTP: Validation error
            HTTP-->>Apollo: Error with details
            Apollo-->>Client: Show validation errors
        else Validation Passed
            Resolver->>Service: Call business method
            Service->>Service: Business logic

            alt Needs Cache
                Service->>Redis: GET key

                alt Cache Hit
                    Redis-->>Service: Cached data
                else Cache Miss
                    Service->>Prisma: Query database
                    Prisma->>DB: SQL query
                    DB-->>Prisma: Query result
                    Prisma-->>Service: Data
                    Service->>Redis: SET key (with TTL)
                end
            else Direct DB Query
                Service->>Prisma: Query/mutation
                Prisma->>DB: SQL operation
                DB-->>Prisma: Result
                Prisma-->>Service: Data
            end

            Service-->>Resolver: Return data
            Resolver->>Resolver: Transform to GraphQL type
            Resolver-->>Server: Response data
        end

        Server->>Server: Serialize response
        Server->>Middleware: GraphQL Logger
        Middleware->>Middleware: Log operation (dev: detailed, prod: compact)

        Server-->>HTTP: GraphQL response
        HTTP-->>Apollo: JSON response
        Apollo->>Apollo: Update cache
        Apollo->>Apollo: Trigger subscriptions
        Apollo-->>Client: Return data
        Client->>Client: Update UI
    end

    %% Subscription Flow
    rect rgb(16, 185, 129, 0.1)
        Note over Client,DB: GraphQL Subscription Flow
        Client->>Apollo: Subscribe to event
        Apollo->>Apollo: Open WebSocket connection
        Apollo->>HTTP: WS handshake /graphql
        HTTP->>Server: WebSocket upgrade
        Server-->>HTTP: Connection established
        HTTP-->>Apollo: WebSocket open
        Apollo->>HTTP: subscription { event }
        HTTP->>Server: Subscription message
        Server->>Server: Register subscription
        Server-->>HTTP: Subscription ID
        HTTP-->>Apollo: Subscribed

        loop Event Occurs
            Note over Resolver,Server: Event triggered
            Resolver->>Server: Publish event
            Server->>Server: Match subscriptions
            Server->>HTTP: Send event data
            HTTP->>Apollo: WebSocket message
            Apollo->>Apollo: Update cache
            Apollo-->>Client: Trigger callback
            Client->>Client: Update UI
        end

        Client->>Apollo: Unsubscribe
        Apollo->>HTTP: Stop subscription
        HTTP->>Server: Unsubscribe message
        Server->>Server: Remove subscription
    end

    %% Error Flow
    rect rgb(220, 38, 38, 0.1)
        Note over Client,DB: Error Handling Flow
        Client->>Apollo: Execute operation
        Apollo->>HTTP: GraphQL request
        HTTP->>Server: Request
        Server->>Resolver: Execute
        Resolver->>Service: Call method

        alt Service Error
            Service->>Service: Throw exception
            Service-->>Resolver: Error
            Resolver->>Resolver: Catch & transform
            Resolver-->>Server: GraphQL error
        else Prisma Error
            Service->>Prisma: Query
            Prisma->>DB: SQL
            DB-->>Prisma: Database error
            Prisma-->>Service: Prisma error
            Service->>Service: Transform error (P2002 → ConflictException)
            Service-->>Resolver: Handled error
            Resolver-->>Server: GraphQL error
        end

        Server->>Server: Format error (hide internals in prod)
        Server->>Middleware: Log error (full stack in dev)
        Server-->>HTTP: Error response (errors array)
        HTTP-->>Apollo: GraphQL errors

        Apollo->>Apollo: onError link
        Apollo->>Apollo: Check error type

        alt Network Error
            Apollo->>Apollo: Retry with exponential backoff
        else Auth Error (401)
            Apollo->>Apollo: Clear cache
            Apollo->>Apollo: Redirect to login
        else Other GraphQL Error
            Apollo-->>Client: Show error message
        end
    end

    %% File Upload Flow
    rect rgb(245, 158, 11, 0.1)
        Note over Client,DB: File Upload Flow (Multipart)
        Client->>Apollo: Upload file mutation
        Apollo->>Apollo: Create multipart request
        Apollo->>HTTP: POST /graphql (multipart/form-data)
        HTTP->>Server: Multipart request
        Server->>Middleware: graphql-upload handler
        Middleware->>Middleware: Parse file stream
        Middleware->>Middleware: Validate file (size, type)

        alt Validation Failed
            Middleware-->>Server: ValidationException
            Server-->>Apollo: Validation error
        else Validation Passed
            Server->>Resolver: Execute with file
            Resolver->>Service: Process file
            Service->>Service: Transform file (Sharp)
            Service->>Service: Upload to Cloudinary
            Service->>Prisma: Save file URL
            Prisma->>DB: UPDATE users SET avatar = ?
            Service-->>Resolver: File URL
            Resolver-->>Server: Response
            Server-->>Apollo: Success
            Apollo-->>Client: Show uploaded file
        end
    end
```

## GraphQL Request Flow Components

### 1. Request Entry
**Apollo Client**:
- Serializes GraphQL query/mutation
- Adds authentication headers (cookies)
- Handles variables and file uploads
- Manages local cache

**HTTP Layer**:
- POST to `/graphql` endpoint
- Content-Type: `application/json` or `multipart/form-data` (uploads)
- Includes session cookie
- WebSocket upgrade for subscriptions

### 2. Middleware Chain
Executed in order:
1. **Helmet**: Security headers (CSP, XSS protection)
2. **i18next**: Language detection from headers/cookies
3. **Body Parser**: JSON parsing
4. **Cookie Parser**: Session cookie extraction
5. **Session Middleware**: Session restoration from Redis
6. **GraphQL Upload**: Multipart file handling

### 3. Apollo Server Processing
**Steps**:
1. Parse GraphQL query string
2. Validate syntax against schema
3. Determine operation type (query, mutation, subscription)
4. Extract operation name and variables
5. Build execution context

**Context Injection**:
```typescript
{
  req: Request,          // Express request
  res: Response,         // Express response
  language: string,      // Detected language
  user?: User           // Populated by auth guard
}
```

### 4. Rate Limiting
**RateLimitGuard**:
- Applies to specific resolvers via `@RateLimit()` decorator
- Uses Redis ZSET for sliding window algorithm
- Tracks attempts per IP (unauthenticated) or userId (authenticated)
- Returns 429 with `Retry-After` header if exceeded

**Rate Limit Headers**:
```
X-RateLimit-Limit: 10
X-RateLimit-Remaining: 7
X-RateLimit-Reset: 1639584000
```

### 5. Authentication Guard
**GqlAuthGuard**:
- Checks for session cookie
- Validates session in Redis
- Fetches user from database
- Attaches user to context
- Throws `UnauthorizedException` if invalid

**Session Validation**:
- Check expiration (`expiresAt`)
- Check revocation (`revokedAt`)
- Update last used timestamp

### 6. Resolver Execution
**Decorators**:
- `@Authorization()`: Apply auth guard
- `@Authorized()`: Inject current user
- `@Lang()`: Inject language
- `@UserAgent()`: Inject user agent
- `@Context()`: Inject full context

**DTO Validation**:
- Class-validator decorators
- Custom validators
- I18n error messages

**Example Resolver**:
```typescript
@Mutation(() => User)
@Authorization()
async updateProfile(
  @Authorized() user: User,
  @Args('data') data: UpdateProfileInput,
  @Lang() lang: string
): Promise<User> {
  return this.service.updateProfile(user.id, data, lang);
}
```

### 7. Service Layer
**Business Logic**:
- Extends `CoreService` for infrastructure access
- Implements business rules
- Calls Prisma for data operations
- Uses Redis for caching

**Caching Strategy**:
- Cache frequently accessed data
- Set appropriate TTLs
- Invalidate on mutations
- Use key namespacing

**Transaction Support**:
```typescript
await this.prisma.$transaction(async (tx) => {
  await tx.user.update(...);
  await tx.auditLog.create(...);
});
```

### 8. Prisma ORM
**Query Building**:
- Type-safe query construction
- Relation loading (include, select)
- Filtering, sorting, pagination
- Aggregations

**Error Handling**:
- `P2002`: Unique constraint violation → `ConflictException`
- `P2025`: Record not found → `NotFoundException`
- `P2003`: Foreign key violation → `BadRequestException`

### 9. Redis Caching
**Operations**:
- `GET/SET`: Simple key-value cache
- `ZADD/ZCOUNT`: Rate limiting (sorted sets)
- `SETEX`: Cache with TTL
- `DEL`: Cache invalidation
- `INCR/DECR`: Counters

**Key Patterns**:
- `user:${userId}`: User cache
- `session:${sessionId}`: Session data
- `ratelimit:${endpoint}:${identifier}`: Rate limit counter

### 10. Response Serialization
**GraphQL Response**:
```typescript
{
  data: {
    // Query/mutation result
  },
  errors: [
    // GraphQL errors (if any)
  ]
}
```

**Error Format**:
```typescript
{
  message: "Error message",
  extensions: {
    code: "UNAUTHENTICATED",
    statusCode: 401
  },
  path: ["fieldName"],
  locations: [{ line: 1, column: 1 }]
}
```

### 11. Logging
**GraphQLLoggerMiddleware**:
- Development: Full query, variables, result
- Production: Operation name, duration, errors only

**Log Format**:
```
[GraphQL] login (123ms) - User login successful
[GraphQL] updateProfile (45ms) - ERROR: Validation failed
```

### 12. Apollo Client Response Handling
**Cache Update**:
- Normalize response data
- Update Apollo cache
- Trigger reactive queries
- Optimistic updates support

**Error Link**:
- Intercept errors
- Handle authentication errors (401 → redirect)
- Network errors (retry with backoff)
- Log errors to console/service

### 13. Subscription Flow
**WebSocket Connection**:
- Initial HTTP upgrade request
- `graphql-ws` protocol
- Connection authentication
- Heartbeat/ping-pong

**Subscription Lifecycle**:
1. Client sends `subscribe` message
2. Server registers subscription
3. Events trigger `pubsub.publish()`
4. Server sends updates to subscribed clients
5. Client receives real-time updates
6. Client sends `complete` to unsubscribe

**Use Cases**:
- Real-time notifications
- Live data updates
- Chat messages
- Status changes

### 14. File Upload Flow
**Multipart Request**:
- `graphql-upload-minimal` library
- Stream processing for large files
- File size limits (configurable)
- MIME type validation

**Upload Process**:
1. Parse multipart form data
2. Validate file (size, type)
3. Stream to temporary storage
4. Process file (resize, compress)
5. Upload to Cloudinary
6. Delete temporary file
7. Save URL in database

**Validation**:
- Max file size: 5MB (configurable)
- Allowed types: image/jpeg, image/png, image/webp
- Filename sanitization

## Performance Optimizations

### Caching
- Redis for session data (fast lookup)
- Apollo Client cache (reduce network requests)
- Database query result caching

### Query Optimization
- Prisma relation loading (avoid N+1)
- Pagination for large datasets
- Field selection (only fetch needed fields)

### Rate Limiting
- Prevent abuse
- Protect against DDoS
- Per-endpoint configuration

### Connection Pooling
- PostgreSQL connection pool (Prisma)
- Redis connection pool

## Security Features

### Input Validation
- DTO validation with class-validator
- SQL injection prevention (Prisma)
- XSS prevention (output escaping)

### Authentication
- Session-based auth
- Cookie security (HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite)
- CSRF protection

### Rate Limiting
- Sliding window algorithm
- Per-user and per-IP tracking
- Configurable limits per endpoint

### Error Handling
- Hide internal errors in production
- Sanitize error messages
- Log full stack traces for debugging
